{"Title":"An Act relative to utility bills","BillNumber":"H3680","DocketNumber":"HD1279","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"R_C1","Name":"Rob Consalvo","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/R_C1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-17T15:56:55.777"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"R_C1","Name":"Rob Consalvo","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/R_C1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-17T15:56:55.7766667"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H3680/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Consalvo of Boston, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 3680) of Rob Consalvo relative to the listing on utility bill of discounts available to seniors, veterans or persons with disabilities.  Telecommunications, Utilities and Energy.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Chapter 165 of the General Laws is hereby amended by inserting after section 11E the following section:-\r\n\tSection 11F. Any city, town, district or company engaged in supplying water to customers shall include a list of all billing discounts available to seniors, veterans or persons with disabilities on every water bill to a customer.\r\n\tSECTION 2. Section 1D of chapter 164 of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2020 Official Edition, is hereby amended by adding the following paragraph:-\r\n\tAll electric and gas bills sent to a retail customer shall include a list of all billing discounts available to seniors, veterans or persons with disabilities.\r\n\tSECTION 3. Chapter 25C of the General Laws is hereby amended by adding the following section:-\r\n\tSection 10. All bills for services provided to consumers by companies subject to the supervision of the department pursuant to section 1 shall include a list of all billing discounts available to seniors, veterans or persons with disabilities.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[],"Amendments":[]}